1
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,170
Yeah,

2
00:00:48,253 --> 00:00:49,083
yeah,

3
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:54,380
yeah.

4
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,340
Don't you, O 'Kaseen?

5
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:33,154
The blood of the children in their body

6
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,073
They want to know how to get rid of them

7
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:46,300
They want to know how to get rid of them

8
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:50,217
Black Wargreymon to fight Wargreymon and

9
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:55,717
Imperial Dramon In the

10
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,700
battle of Black Wargreymon,
what would you say?

11
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,337
Don't you think they
make mittens for wings?

12
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,357
We need a more permanent solution.

13
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:25,322
Otherwise, Digimon like Daemon will keep
trying to break through to the real world.

14
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,497
Despite reports that monsters
have been appearing worldwide,

15
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,177
government agencies have
been hesitant to respond.

16
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:36,057
They've dismissed these sightings as the
work of practical jokers and goofballs.

17
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:39,537
However, recent incidents have prompted
officials to take the issue seriously.

18
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:41,057
In a press conference today,

19
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,857
it was revealed that
the so-called monsters

20
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,857
would be considered
unidentified life forms.

21
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:48,437
The Home Defense Force is expected
to head up the investigation.

22
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,461
In the meantime,

23
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:53,699
the public is being strongly cautioned
not to panic and to stay calm.

24
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:56,237
So don't monster-proof
your homes yet, folks.

25
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:59,438
They say that it's probably
nothing but a silly hoax.

26
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,160
Cody, did you hear a noise?

27
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,085
It's just my stomach growling.

28
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:08,300
I think I hear it coming
from somewhere down there.

29
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,237
Hey, it took my prune juice!

30
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,960
Uh-oh, I made a boo-boo.

31
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,120
And it can talk.

32
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:19,297
When food's put in front of
me, I just can't help myself.

33
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:20,210
Sorry.

34
00:03:20,293 --> 00:03:21,320
We all make mistakes.

35
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,737
Grandpa, I'm sorry for keeping this
from you, but it's just that I...

36
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,650
What?

37
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:27,297
I knew there was something fishy going on.

38
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:28,597
What do you mean by that?

39
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:31,637
That stuffed animal's got more
than cotton balls in his stomach.

40
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,550
Uh...

41
00:03:32,633 --> 00:03:33,463
You can't fool me.

42
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:34,376
Huh?

43
00:03:34,459 --> 00:03:35,617
Let me guess, he's not from this world.

44
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,237
He's been transported from another
dimension, maybe a digital one.

45
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:40,957
Am I hearing you right, Grandpa?

46
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,260
You know about the digital world?

47
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,757
How'd you find out about it?

48
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:47,840
So, that's what you kids
are calling it these days.

49
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,357
Well, I suppose it was
only a matter of time.

50
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:54,757
I knew I'd have to tell you at some point,
but I didn't expect to do it so soon.

51
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,997
You see, Cody, it has to do with your dad.

52
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,437
When he was just a young rascal like you,

53
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:03,137
he always talked about going to some
strange place like a digital world.

54
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:05,137
You mean my dad knew about it too?

55
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,777
I didn't think too much of it at first,

56
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:10,197
because he was always interested in
video games and things of that sort,

57
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:14,437
But suddenly he started doing things
that really worried me Sometimes

58
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,837
he'd be playing a game And he'd act
like he was seeing things that no

59
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,777
one else did As if the characters
actually came to life He'd sit at

60
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:26,154
that TV for hours in a trance Sometimes
he'd even carry on conversations,

61
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:30,197
I thought, with himself It gave me the
willies, if you want to know the truth

62
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,320
Dad did that?

63
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:35,304
I thought he was playing around,
but he knew they were real Cody!

64
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,370
Huh?

65
00:04:36,453 --> 00:04:39,897
I hope you're not planning on going
out again by yourself Oh, come on,

66
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:43,437
Mom Please no you've been out every
day this week and with all this talk

67
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:47,377
about monsters it worries me I'd
rather you stay at home today honey.

68
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:51,057
Nothing's gonna happen besides my
friends are expecting me You worry

69
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:55,022
too much all that monster talk is
probably just rumors and hearsay

70
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,100
He'll be in good hands.

71
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:59,117
He and I are going to
go practice our kendo.

72
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:01,024
I'll keep an eye on him, right?

73
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:04,057
Those despicable Digidestined
have been snooping

74
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:07,140
around keeping tabs on all
the other little urchins

75
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,498
Fortunately for us,

76
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:12,117
the dark spores have begun to take
root in their teensy little brains.

77
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,737
But there's a slight complication.

78
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,650
What now?

79
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,477
There's one brat whose spore
is about to sprout early.

80
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,537
That could be trouble.

81
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:19,679
What should we do?

82
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:25,249
Without the dark spore, I'd
just become an ordinary bumpkin.

83
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:28,260
Small potatoes doomed
to a life of mediocrity.

84
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,897
Now I'll be able to rise above the crowd.

85
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,357
Oh, there you are, honey.

86
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,220
What are you up to? Can I see?

87
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,380
I'm busy.

88
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:44,964
How am I supposed to achieve perfection
if inferior people keep trying to butt in?

89
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:47,060
It's very frustrating.

90
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,480
I'm sorry to be late.

91
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,757
My mom was worried and
didn't want me to leave.

92
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,717
I don't blame her, but
I'm sure glad you're here.

93
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,917
I'm ready for a break.

94
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,177
You'd better go get something to eat
before it's time for the next shift.

95
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:01,300
A chocolate bar is calling
out my name. See ya!

96
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,497
You mind bringing me back something?

97
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,517
I'd be delighted.

98
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,430
How about quiche?

99
00:06:05,513 --> 00:06:08,737
I don't care if it's quiched or
squashed, as long as it's edible.

100
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:09,660
My book!

101
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,720
Uh-oh. Here it is.

102
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:12,817
I need to leave my things alone!

103
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:13,730
Now go away!

104
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:14,677
You're interrupting me!

105
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,077
I just wanted to see if you
needed any help, that's all.

106
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,280
No, no, no!

107
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,300
This is bad.

108
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:22,220
That spore's growing fast.

109
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,337
You're right about that.

110
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:25,137
She could break glass with that scream.

111
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:28,237
If she's giving me a headache,
imagine how her mama feels.

112
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,150
Excellent.

113
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,657
She's progressing very nicely, and
there's nothing you can do about it.

114
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:34,177
So just go home. No way!

115
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:35,090
I'm not moving!

116
00:06:35,173 --> 00:06:38,097
Don't you know that people who
don't move never get ahead in life?

117
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:39,010
What's the matter?

118
00:06:39,093 --> 00:06:40,477
You afraid to improve your mind?

119
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,460
Come on, why be merely ordinary?

120
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,077
It's better than being
controlled by a fiend.

121
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:46,377
Nobody is being controlled.

122
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:47,757
They all asked for it.

123
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,297
All I did is grant their wishes.

124
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,477
Perhaps you're just jealous that
they'll become more powerful than you.

125
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:54,757
If you happen to change
your mind, let me know.

126
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,597
In the meantime, don't
attempt to interfere.

127
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,057
They've made their choice and
it's too late to turn back.

128
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:00,277
How could they make a choice?

129
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,190
You're lying.

130
00:07:01,273 --> 00:07:02,137
They've been brainwashed.

131
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:04,097
You made them all a
bunch of false promises.

132
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,637
You say they're going to
become superior beings,

133
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,477
but you don't even know what that means.

134
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:11,437
A superior being is someone who
helps and cares about others.

135
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,755
The name on that bag.

136
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,420
It says Hida.

137
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,410
Hiroki.

138
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,080
That was my dad's name.

139
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,010
What's it to you?

140
00:07:19,093 --> 00:07:20,577
I believe we have a problem.

141
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,248
There goes our lunch break.

142
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,981
We'll eliminate that little twit.

143
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:26,477
Guess I'll have to eat later.

144
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,757
You won't feel like it when
we are finished with you.

145
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,781
Get out of here.

146
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,817
Don't just stand there like
a couple of silly fools.

147
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:34,076
I gave you an order.

148
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:36,651
Well, he could have at least said, please.

149
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:37,590
Really?

150
00:07:37,673 --> 00:07:39,260
Go, do as I say. Ingrate.

151
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,160
Hiroki-san.

152
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,600
He's similar in so many ways.

153
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:51,348
But I can't let myself give in
to weakness when I'm so close.

154
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,320
Oh, Hiroki.

155
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:03,137
I had a vision for the future
that everyone said was impossible.

156
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:06,080
But you always encouraged
me to keep trying.

157
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,730
Yeah.

158
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:12,520
I never fit in as a kid.

159
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:15,297
They all laughed at me
and thought I was strange.

160
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,674
You never did, though.

161
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,647
It was as if we were
made from the same mold.

162
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,960
Why should I care? He's gone.

163
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:29,660
What a fool I was.

164
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,237
Happiness is an illusion.

165
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:32,740
Life's ugly and cruel.

166
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,340
I've moved on.

167
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,618
So why has he come back to haunt me?

168
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,040
He's dead.

169
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,897
I can't let his memory
keep me from my destiny.

170
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:42,177
You won't change my mind.

171
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:43,320
I won't let you!

172
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:51,080
If there was only some way I could
show you the virtual beings I created,

173
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,797
you'd understand what
I'm about to accomplish.

174
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:56,340
I made digital copies of my own DNA.

175
00:08:56,700 --> 00:09:01,217
The copies were computer-generated into
solid images of my own genetic essence.

176
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,130
Well,

177
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,957
you'll never win a beauty
contest But after all,

178
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:09,864
it's what's inside that counts And that's
not much What are you trying to tell me?

179
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:13,777
You're horrid and empty, so
get over it You're baiting me,

180
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,720
now stop it What's the matter?

181
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,297
Afraid to face the truth?

182
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:21,337
We represent the essence of
your ugliness We're living your

183
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:26,540
nightmare Lies You were just
a foreign object You're wrong!

184
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:31,820
It's mind-boggling.

185
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:35,437
We had the perfect opportunity to lift
those kids in the butt, and he stopped us.

186
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,517
What was he thinking?

187
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,857
He's two tacos short of a combo platter.

188
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:42,417
I can't help but remember that
conversation with Blackmore Koromon.

189
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:46,217
He's a Digimon, and Oikawa's a
human, so what are we supposed to be?

190
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,130
Chopped liver?

191
00:09:47,213 --> 00:09:48,043
Virtual viruses?

192
00:09:48,126 --> 00:09:49,217
Horror film wannabes?

193
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:53,297
I'm telling you, my dear, this is
giving me a vast feeling of inferiority.

194
00:09:53,380 --> 00:09:56,737
Did I ever mention you're
thoroughly pathetic when you whine?

195
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:57,917
We'll get to the bottom of it.

196
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,217
In the meantime, quit your harping.

197
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,460
You're exasperating me.

198
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:04,378
I'll see you later.

199
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:06,480
Be careful out there. I will.

200
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:09,680
Grandpa. What is it? I need to know.

201
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:12,058
Would you say my dad was a good guy?

202
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,300
Your dad was a very good guy.

203
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:16,117
He was as good as they come.

204
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,557
Why would you ask me
something like that, Cody?

205
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:21,297
I met a man yesterday who
said that he'd known him.

206
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:23,177
I was just curious about it, that's all.

207
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:24,090
Is that so?

208
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,457
What was the man's name?

209
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:28,660
He told me his name was Oikawa. Really?

210
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,580
Well, that's very interesting.

211
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,237
You're Ken Ichijoji, aren't you?

212
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,150
What do you want?

213
00:10:47,233 --> 00:10:48,657
Don't you know that spying is rude?

214
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:50,211
I'm sorry I followed you.

215
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,560
Just hear me out.

216
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,317
There's something you need to
know about before it's too late.

217
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,837
Something I need to know?

218
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:58,177
Oh, please, why should I
care what you have to say?

219
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:01,357
Now that you're an ordinary kid
again, you're just an insect to me.

220
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,270
You gave it all off.

221
00:11:02,353 --> 00:11:03,717
The brains, the power, and for what?

222
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,757
So people would like you?

223
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,428
No, so I would like myself.

224
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,257
Power gave me nothing but loneliness.

225
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:09,857
You have to believe me, Noriko.

226
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,157
This isn't the answer.

227
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,677
I suppose you're going to tell me that the

228
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:14,637
answer is having friends
and parents who love you,

229
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,550
right?

230
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,463
Give me a break.

231
00:11:16,546 --> 00:11:17,376
That's just sad.

232
00:11:17,459 --> 00:11:18,617
I bet you don't even
believe what you're saying.

233
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,053
I'm sure not buying it.

234
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,957
This is going to be harder than I
thought, but I have to keep trying.

235
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:26,040
I can't let her suffer like I did.

236
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:28,417
I'm out of here, so do me a favor.

237
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:31,500
Bug off, insect boy. Yo, Ken. Hey, dude.

238
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:35,080
Hey, what's with her? Don't ask.

239
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,300
Uh-oh. Huh?

240
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:49,317
Boy, you really must have made her mad.

241
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,230
Okay.

242
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:26,590
Huh?

243
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:30,440
Uwekawa and his fan club.

244
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:31,597
What do they want?

245
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:35,400
You get three guesses and
they're all her. No way. Right!

246
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:40,380
Wyrm-on Digibolb-doo!

247
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,190
Digibolb!

248
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,640
Beem-on Digibolb-doo!

249
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,620
And Beem-on Digibolb-doo!

250
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:57,280
EXP-MOD!

251
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:01,260
STEN-MOD!

252
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,900
DEAN-AN DIGITAL 2!

253
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:09,860
IELDRAGON!

254
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:16,700
TESTING!

